[32;1m[1;3mQuestion: A consumer electronics factory operates an assembly line with three workstations and can produce 101 premium radio models: HiFi-1, HiFi-2, …, HiFi-101. The processing time required per unit of each model at each workstation is provided in workstation_times.csv. Each workstation has 1,440 minutes of total daily time. Daily maintenance consumes 10% of the available time at workstation 1, 14% at workstation 2, and 12% at workstation 3, so production may use only the remaining effective capacity of each workstation. Determine the nonnegative integer number of units of each radio model to produce per day so as to minimize total idle production time across the three workstations. For each workstation, idle time is its effective daily capacity minus the total processing time used at that workstation.

Thought: I need to retrieve all processing times per model and workstation from workstation_times.csv, and use the maintenance percentages and total time to compute effective capacities. The variables are the integer number of units of each model to produce. The objective is to minimize the sum of idle times across all workstations, where idle time at each workstation is its effective capacity minus the total processing time used. All variables must be nonnegative integers.

Action: CSVQA

Action Input: Retrieve all data from workstation_times.csv, preserving source order and all identifiers and values.
